WEBVTT

00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:02.078
Define a Fabric ontology in plain

00:00:02.078 --> 00:00:02.839
language.

00:00:03.809 --> 00:00:04.931
It's a shared model of the

00:00:04.931 --> 00:00:06.713
things the business cares about,

00:00:06.717 --> 00:00:08.005
what we know about them,

00:00:08.005 --> 00:00:09.047
how they connect,

00:00:09.077 --> 00:00:11.050
and where the supporting data lives.

00:00:12.029 --> 00:00:13.696
A Store is an entity type.

00:00:14.657 --> 00:00:16.809
A particular store is an instance.

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:19.966
Region and priority are properties.

00:00:20.945 --> 00:00:23.050
“Store operates Refrigeration Unit” is a

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.155
relationship.

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:27.340
A data binding connects those concepts

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.006
to actual source fields.

00:00:29.969 --> 00:00:31.742
We can also attach business rules

00:00:31.742 --> 00:00:32.758
and metrics.

00:00:33.725 --> 00:00:35.205
That lets a question refer to

00:00:35.205 --> 00:00:37.615
an established concept instead of asking

00:00:37.615 --> 00:00:39.796
every consumer to reconstruct its meaning

00:00:39.796 --> 00:00:41.030
from table names.
